nvim_get_runtime_file({name}, {all})                 *nvim_get_runtime_file()*
    Finds files in runtime directories, in 'runtimepath' order.

    "name" can contain wildcards. For example
    `nvim_get_runtime_file("colors/*.{vim,lua}", true)` will return all color
    scheme files. Always use forward slashes (/) in the search pattern for
    subdirectories regardless of platform.

    It is not an error to not find any files. An empty array is returned then.

    Attributes: ~
        |api-fast|
        Since: 0.5.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {name}  (`string`) pattern of files to search for
      ‚Ä¢ {all}   (`boolean`) whether to return all matches or only the first

    Return: ~
        (`string[]`) list of absolute paths to the found files

