    Sets the current tabpage.

    Attributes: ~
        not allowed when |textlock| is active
        Since: 0.1.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {tabpage}  (`integer`) |tab-ID| to focus

nvim_set_current_win({win})                           *nvim_set_current_win()*
    Navigates to the given window (and tabpage, implicitly).

    Attributes: ~
        not allowed when |textlock| is active
        Since: 0.1.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {win}  (`integer`) |window-ID| to focus

nvim_set_hl({ns_id}, {name}, {val})                            *nvim_set_hl()*
    Sets a highlight group. By default, replaces the entire definition (e.g.
    `nvim_set_hl(0, 'Visual', {})` will clear the "Visual" group), unless
    `update` is specified.

    Note: ~
      ‚Ä¢ The fg and bg keys also accept the string values `"fg"` or `"bg"`
        which act as aliases to the corresponding foreground and background
        values of the Normal group. If the Normal group has not been defined,
        using these values results in an error.
      ‚Ä¢ If `link` is used in combination with other attributes; only the
        `link` will take effect (see |:hi-link|).

    Attributes: ~
        Since: 0.5.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {ns_id}  (`integer`) Namespace id for this highlight
                 |nvim_create_namespace()|. Use 0 to set a highlight group
                 globally |:highlight|. Highlights from non-global namespaces
                 are not active by default, use |nvim_set_hl_ns()| or
                 |nvim_win_set_hl_ns()| to activate them.
      ‚Ä¢ {name}   (`string`) Highlight group name, e.g. "ErrorMsg"
      ‚Ä¢ {val}    (`vim.api.keyset.highlight`) Highlight definition map,
                 accepts the following keys:
                 ‚Ä¢ altfont: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ bg: color name or "#RRGGBB", see note.
                 ‚Ä¢ bg_indexed: boolean. If true, `bg` is an RGB approximation
                   of `ctermbg` (a palette index). UIs rendering cterm
                   natively may prefer `ctermbg`.
                 ‚Ä¢ blend: integer between 0 and 100
                 ‚Ä¢ blink: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ bold: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ conceal: boolean Concealment at the UI level (terminal
                   SGR), unrelated to |:syn-conceal|.
                 ‚Ä¢ cterm: cterm attribute map, like |highlight-args|. If not
                   set, cterm attributes will match those from the attribute
                   map documented above.
                 ‚Ä¢ ctermbg: Sets background of cterm color |ctermbg|
                 ‚Ä¢ ctermfg: Sets foreground of cterm color |ctermfg|
                 ‚Ä¢ default: boolean Don't override existing definition
                   |:hi-default|
                 ‚Ä¢ dim: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ fg: Color name or "#RRGGBB", see note.
                 ‚Ä¢ fg_indexed: boolean. Same as `bg_indexed`, for `fg` and
                   `ctermfg`.
                 ‚Ä¢ font: GUI font name (string). Sets |highlight-font|. Use
                   "NONE" to clear.
                 ‚Ä¢ force: (boolean, default: false) Update the highlight group
                   even if it already exists.
                 ‚Ä¢ italic: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ link: Name of highlight group to link to. |:hi-link|
                 ‚Ä¢ link_global: Like "link", but always resolved in the global
                   namespace (ns=0).
                 ‚Ä¢ nocombine: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ overline: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ reverse: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ sp: Color name or "#RRGGBB"
                 ‚Ä¢ standout: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ strikethrough: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ undercurl: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ underdashed: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ underdotted: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ underdouble: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ underline: boolean
                 ‚Ä¢ update: (boolean, default: false) Update specified
                   attributes only, leave others unchanged.

nvim_set_hl_ns({ns_id})                                     *nvim_set_hl_ns()*
    Set active namespace for highlights defined with |nvim_set_hl()|. This can
    be set for a single window, see |nvim_win_set_hl_ns()|.

    Attributes: ~
        Since: 0.8.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {ns_id}  (`integer`) the namespace to use

nvim_set_hl_ns_fast({ns_id})                           *nvim_set_hl_ns_fast()*
    Set active namespace for highlights defined with |nvim_set_hl()| while
    redrawing.

    This function is meant to be called while redrawing, primarily from
    |nvim_set_decoration_provider()| on_win and on_line callbacks, which are
    allowed to change the namespace during a redraw cycle.

    Attributes: ~
        |api-fast|
        Since: 0.8.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {ns_id}  (`integer`) the namespace to activate

nvim_set_keymap({mode}, {lhs}, {rhs}, {opts})              *nvim_set_keymap()*
    Sets a global |mapping| for the given mode.

    To set a buffer-local mapping, use |nvim_buf_set_keymap()|.

    Unlike |:map|, leading/trailing whitespace is accepted as part of the
    {lhs} or {rhs}. Empty {rhs} is <Nop>. |keycodes| are replaced as usual.

    Example: >vim
        call nvim_set_keymap('n', ' <NL>', '', {'nowait': v:true})
<

    is equivalent to: >vim
        nmap <nowait> <Space><NL> <Nop>
<

    Attributes: ~
        Since: 0.4.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {mode}  (`string`) Mode short-name (map command prefix: "n", "i", "v",
                "x", ‚Ä¶) or "!" for |:map!|, or empty string for |:map|.
                "ia", "ca" or "!a" for abbreviation in Insert mode, Cmdline
                mode, or both, respectively
      ‚Ä¢ {lhs}   (`string`) Left-hand-side |{lhs}| of the mapping.
      ‚Ä¢ {rhs}   (`string`) Right-hand-side |{rhs}| of the mapping.
      ‚Ä¢ {opts}  (`vim.api.keyset.keymap?`) Optional parameters map: Accepts
                all |:map-arguments| as keys except <buffer>, values are
                booleans (default false). Also:
                ‚Ä¢ "callback" Lua function called in place of {rhs}.
                ‚Ä¢ "desc" human-readable description.
                ‚Ä¢ "noremap" disables |recursive_mapping|, like |:noremap|
                ‚Ä¢ "replace_keycodes" (boolean) When "expr" is true, replace
                  keycodes in the resulting string (see
                  |nvim_replace_termcodes()|). Returning nil from the Lua
                  "callback" is equivalent to returning an empty string.

