nvim__redraw({opts})                                          *nvim__redraw()*
    WARNING: This feature is experimental/unstable.

    Instruct Nvim to redraw various components.

    Attributes: ~
        Since: 0.10.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {opts}  (`vim.api.keyset.redraw?`) Optional parameters.
                ‚Ä¢ buf: Target a specific buffer number as described below.
                ‚Ä¢ cursor: Immediately update cursor position on the screen in
                  `win` or the current window.
                ‚Ä¢ flush: Update the screen with pending updates.
                ‚Ä¢ range: Redraw a range in `buf`, the buffer in `win` or the
                  current buffer (useful for decoration providers). Expects a
                  tuple `[first, last]` with the first and last line number of
                  the range, 0-based end-exclusive |api-indexing|.
                ‚Ä¢ statuscolumn: Redraw the 'statuscolumn' in `buf`, `win` or
                  all windows.
                ‚Ä¢ statusline: Redraw the 'statusline' in `buf`, `win` or all
                  windows.
                ‚Ä¢ tabline: Redraw the 'tabline'.
                ‚Ä¢ valid: When present mark `win`, `buf`, or all windows for
                  redraw. When `true`, only redraw changed lines (useful for
                  decoration providers). When `false`, forcefully redraw.
                ‚Ä¢ win: Target a specific |window-ID| as described below.
                ‚Ä¢ winbar: Redraw the 'winbar' in `buf`, `win` or all windows.

    See also: ~
      ‚Ä¢ |:redraw|

