Lua module: vim.inspector                                      *vim.inspector*

vim.inspect_pos({buf}, {row}, {col}, {filter})             *vim.inspect_pos()*
    Get all the items at a given buffer position.

    Can also be pretty-printed with `:Inspect!`.                   *:Inspect!*

    Attributes: ~
        Since: 0.9.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {buf}     (`integer?`) defaults to the current buffer
      ‚Ä¢ {row}     (`integer?`) row to inspect, 0-based. Defaults to the row of
                  the current cursor
      ‚Ä¢ {col}     (`integer?`) col to inspect, 0-based. Defaults to the col of
                  the current cursor
      ‚Ä¢ {filter}  (`table?`) Table with key-value pairs to filter the items
                  ‚Ä¢ {extmarks} (`boolean|"all"`, default: true) Include
                    extmarks. When `all`, then extmarks without a `hl_group`
                    will also be included.
                  ‚Ä¢ {semantic_tokens} (`boolean`, default: true) Include
                    semantic token highlights.
                  ‚Ä¢ {syntax} (`boolean`, default: `true`) Include syntax based
                    highlight groups.
                  ‚Ä¢ {treesitter} (`boolean`, default: `true`) Include
                    treesitter based highlight groups.

    Return: ~
        (`table`) a table with the following key-value pairs. Items are in
        "traversal order":
        ‚Ä¢ treesitter: a list of treesitter captures
        ‚Ä¢ syntax: a list of syntax groups
        ‚Ä¢ semantic_tokens: a list of semantic tokens
        ‚Ä¢ extmarks: a list of extmarks
        ‚Ä¢ buffer: the buffer used to get the items
        ‚Ä¢ row: the row used to get the items
        ‚Ä¢ col: the col used to get the items

vim.show_pos({buf}, {row}, {col}, {filter})                   *vim.show_pos()*
    Show all the items at a given buffer position.

    Can also be shown with `:Inspect`.                              *:Inspect*

    See also |:marks| to list all extmarks.

    Example: To bind this function to the vim-scriptease inspired `zS` in
    Normal mode: >lua
        vim.keymap.set('n', 'zS', vim.show_pos)
<

    Attributes: ~
        Since: 0.9.0

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {buf}     (`integer?`) defaults to the current buffer
      ‚Ä¢ {row}     (`integer?`) row to inspect, 0-based. Defaults to the row of
                  the current cursor
      ‚Ä¢ {col}     (`integer?`) col to inspect, 0-based. Defaults to the col of
                  the current cursor
      ‚Ä¢ {filter}  (`table?`) A table with the following fields:
                  ‚Ä¢ {extmarks} (`boolean|"all"`, default: true) Include
                    extmarks. When `all`, then extmarks without a `hl_group`
                    will also be included.
                  ‚Ä¢ {semantic_tokens} (`boolean`, default: true) Include
                    semantic token highlights.
                  ‚Ä¢ {syntax} (`boolean`, default: `true`) Include syntax based
                    highlight groups.
                  ‚Ä¢ {treesitter} (`boolean`, default: `true`) Include
                    treesitter based highlight groups.


