Lua module: vim.loader                                            *vim.loader*

vim.loader.enable({enable})                              *vim.loader.enable()*
    WARNING: This feature is experimental/unstable.

    Enables or disables the experimental Lua module loader:

    Enable (`enable=true`):
    ‚Ä¢ overrides |loadfile()|
    ‚Ä¢ adds the Lua loader using the byte-compilation cache
    ‚Ä¢ adds the libs loader
    ‚Ä¢ removes the default Nvim loader

    Disable (`enable=false`):
    ‚Ä¢ removes the loaders
    ‚Ä¢ adds the default Nvim loader

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {enable}  (`boolean?`) true/nil to enable, false to disable

vim.loader.find({modname}, {opts})                         *vim.loader.find()*
    WARNING: This feature is experimental/unstable.

    Finds Lua modules for the given module name.

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {modname}  (`string`) Module name, or `"*"` to find the top-level
                   modules instead
      ‚Ä¢ {opts}     (`table?`) Options for finding a module:
                   ‚Ä¢ {all}? (`boolean`, default: `false`) Search for all
                     matches.
                   ‚Ä¢ {paths}? (`string[]`, default: `{}`) Extra paths to
                     search for modname
                   ‚Ä¢ {patterns}? (`string[]`, default:
                     `{"/init.lua", ".lua"}`) List of patterns to use when
                     searching for modules. A pattern is a string added to the
                     basename of the Lua module being searched.
                   ‚Ä¢ {rtp}? (`boolean`, default: `true`) Search for modname in
                     the runtime path.

    Return: ~
        (`table[]`) A list of objects with the following fields:
        ‚Ä¢ {modname} (`string`) Name of the module
        ‚Ä¢ {modpath} (`string`) Path of the module
        ‚Ä¢ {stat}? (`uv.fs_stat.result`) The fs_stat of the module path. Won't
          be returned for `modname="*"`

vim.loader.reset({path})                                  *vim.loader.reset()*
    WARNING: This feature is experimental/unstable.

    Resets the cache for the path, or all the paths if path is nil.

    Parameters: ~
      ‚Ä¢ {path}  (`string?`) path to reset


